"""Longer user messages for seed_c (same order as seed_c.C), so the user history is far larger than the session context."""
U = [
 ["I'm trying to cook more at home this year instead of ordering in three nights a week. Theo works late on Wednesdays so it's often just me, and I keep defaulting to pasta because it's fast. Any easy weeknight dinners that aren't pasta again? Ideally under 40 minutes and not a ton of dishes.",
  "Fish is fine but I have to be careful: I found out last spring that I'm allergic to shellfish. Shrimp and crab sent me to urgent care with hives and a swollen throat, so anything with shellfish is completely out for me now, including in restaurants.",
  "Good point about oyster sauce, I hadn't thought of that at all. I make a lot of quick stir fries with whatever vegetables are left at the end of the week. What's a substitute I can use that still gives that savoury, slightly sweet flavour?",
  "Perfect. I'll grab some this weekend when I do the big grocery run at the Asian market on South 38th, they have a huge sauce aisle and I usually get lost in there for half an hour anyway.",
  "One more thing while we're on it: do you think I should carry an epinephrine pen? The urgent care doctor mentioned it in passing but I never followed up, and I keep forgetting to ask my regular doctor about it."],
 ["My niece Priya turns seven on March 3rd and she is completely obsessed with octopuses right now. She draws them on everything, she named her goldfish Inky, and she corrects adults who call the arms tentacles. Any gift ideas that aren't just another toy?",
  "An aquarium trip is a great idea. The one at Point Defiance has a giant Pacific octopus, and it's only about twenty minutes from my place, so I could take her on a Saturday when she visits. Do you think seven is old enough to really enjoy it?",
  "Should I get her something to unwrap too? Kids that age seem to care a lot about the actual unwrapping moment on the day, and the trip itself might be a few weeks after her birthday depending on everyone's schedules.",
  "Her mom, my sister Leena, says Priya already has too many plushies and that their apartment is overflowing with stuffed animals. Leena asked everyone to go easy on physical stuff this year, which is fair given how small their place is.",
  "Okay, the aquarium plus a book it is. I'll look for a good octopus book at the library sale and the independent bookstore downtown. Thanks for helping me think this through, I always leave birthday presents to the last minute."],
 ["I finally bought a bike! A used green 2019 Trek FX 2. I paid $340 for it from a guy in Fircrest who was moving to Arizona. It has a few scratches but the ride felt smooth on the test loop around his block. I haven't owned a bike since college.",
  "What should I check first since it's used? I don't really know anything about bike maintenance. The seller said he'd ridden it maybe a few hundred miles total but I have no way of knowing if that's true or how he stored it.",
  "The chain looks a little rusty, especially on the bottom side, and it squeaks a bit when I pedal backwards. The rest of the bike looks okay to me, but I wasn't sure if the rust means I need a whole new chain or if it can be cleaned up.",
  "Do I need a special lock? I'm planning to ride it to the library and the farmers market, and sometimes to the coffee shop near work, so it'll be parked outside for an hour or two at a time on busy streets.",
  "Thanks, I'll get a U-lock this week. I also want to write down the serial number somewhere safe, so I'll take a photo of it on the frame and keep it with my other important documents."],
 ["I want to get back into Spanish. I took three years of it in high school but forgot most of it, and Theo and I are thinking about a trip to Mexico City sometime next year. I'd love to be able to do more than order coffee.",
  "Any podcast recommendations for that? I have a 25-minute drive to the field office twice a week and usually just listen to the radio, so that time could easily go to Spanish instead.",
  "Should I focus on grammar or vocabulary first? In high school it was all verb conjugation tables and I hated it, which is probably part of why none of it stuck. I want to do it differently this time.",
  "How long until I can hold a basic conversation, realistically? I don't need to be fluent, I just want to chat with a taxi driver or a shop owner without freezing up or switching to English after two sentences.",
  "Okay, I'll try fifteen minutes a day and see if I can keep it up through the holidays. I'm usually good for about two weeks with new habits and then something at work blows up and I drop everything."],
 ["I joined a Tuesday night rec volleyball league with some people from work. I haven't played since I was maybe nineteen, and back then I was mostly the person who cheered from the bench, so this is a bit of an adventure.",
  "My forearms are covered in bruises from passing after just one night. Is that normal? They look kind of dramatic and Theo asked if I'd been in a fight. They don't hurt much, they just look bad.",
  "Any tips for serving? Mine keep going straight into the net, and I could feel the whole team silently willing it over every time. I tried overhand once and it went sideways into the next court.",
  "We lost all three sets, but honestly it was really fun, and we went for tacos afterwards. The other team was clearly people who play every week, so I don't feel too bad about it.",
  "Should I stretch before playing? I felt pretty stiff the next morning, especially my shoulders and calves, and I'd like to avoid pulling something before the season is even halfway done."],
 ["I have to write a summary of our flood modelling results for the county board next month. They're smart people but not technical at all, and last time an engineer presented, half of them were on their phones by slide three.",
  "How do I explain a 100-year flood without people thinking it only happens once a century? Every single time I say that phrase someone says 'well we had one in 2007 so we're fine for a while', and it drives me up the wall.",
  "That mortgage framing is really good, I'm stealing it. Should I include maps? We have a lot of them, but they're very busy GIS outputs with twenty layers and a legend the size of a postcard.",
  "How long should the summary be? My manager says 'short' but our last report to them was forty pages plus appendices, and I honestly don't think anyone read past the executive summary.",
  "Thanks, that helps a lot. I'm going to draft the two-page version this week and run it past my manager before the board packet deadline on the 20th."],
 ["My pothos has yellow leaves, maybe five or six of them in the last couple of weeks. It's the one plant I've managed to keep alive for more than a year, so I'm a little attached to it. What am I doing wrong?",
  "It's in a pretty ceramic pot without a drainage hole, which I bought because it matched the bookshelf. I water it about once a week with a full glass of water, sometimes a bit more if I remember it's been a while.",
  "Should I cut off the yellow leaves or wait to see if they recover? Some of them are only partly yellow, with green near the stem, and I don't want to strip the poor thing bare if it's going to bounce back.",
  "It sits near a north-facing window in the living room, on a shelf about four feet from the glass. Is that enough light, or should I move it somewhere brighter? The south side of the apartment gets very hot in summer.",
  "Great, I'll repot it this weekend. I think I have an old plastic nursery pot in the garage that would fit inside the ceramic one, so I can keep the pretty pot on the shelf and still have drainage."],
 ["Biscuit, my corgi, keeps pulling on the leash on every walk, especially when he sees other dogs or squirrels. He's three and otherwise pretty well behaved, but my shoulder is starting to hate our morning walks. Any tips?",
  "He's very food motivated. Honestly, he would do anything for a piece of cheese, and he knows the sound of the treat bag from across the house. He also sits instantly whenever he hears the fridge open.",
  "Should I use a harness instead of a collar? I've read conflicting things online, and the pet store guy tried to sell me a really expensive one with a lot of straps that Biscuit immediately tried to eat.",
  "How long should our walks be? Right now we do about twenty minutes in the morning and a longer one in the evening if it isn't pouring. He seems happy, but he's getting a little round around the middle.",
  "Okay, I'll try a front-clip harness and keep the treats only for walks. I'll report back if he stops dragging me toward every squirrel in the neighbourhood, but I'm not holding my breath."],
 ["I want to start a monthly budget. I make decent money, but somehow at the end of the month I can never really say where it all went, and my savings account has barely moved this year. Where do I begin?",
  "Is the 50/30/20 rule realistic? Our rent alone is almost 40 percent of my take-home pay, and Theo and I split everything evenly, so I'm not sure how much room that leaves for everything else.",
  "Should I use an app or a spreadsheet? I tried one of the popular apps last year but it kept miscategorising things and I got annoyed fixing them every week, so I stopped opening it after a month.",
  "What about an emergency fund? I have a little bit saved, maybe a month of expenses, but my car is old and I'm always half expecting a big repair bill to land on me out of nowhere.",
  "Okay, I'll track this month first before setting any targets. I'll use a simple spreadsheet and check it every Sunday evening while Biscuit has his after-dinner nap."],
 ["I can't fall asleep lately. My mind keeps racing at night, going over work things, emails I forgot to send, the board report, random stuff from years ago. It's been maybe two or three weeks of this now.",
  "I do look at my phone in bed a lot, if I'm honest. I tell myself it's just to check tomorrow's weather, and then it's 12:40 and I've read about the entire history of lighthouses or something equally pointless.",
  "Is it bad to read in bed? I used to read novels before sleep all the time and it always made me drowsy, but I stopped at some point and replaced it with scrolling, which is obviously not an improvement.",
  "What about melatonin? A friend swears by it and said she takes it every night, but I'm wary of starting something every night without knowing more about it or whether it interacts with anything.",
  "I'll try the phone-outside-the-room thing starting tonight. I'll need an actual alarm clock, which feels very retro, but I think I still have one in a drawer from my old apartment."],
 ["Theo's birthday is coming up in a few weeks. He's my partner, we've been together six years. I want to plan something low-key, because he hates surprise parties and being the centre of attention in big groups.",
  "He loves board games and Thai food. Our usual date night is pad see ew from the place down the street and a game of something at the kitchen table, so I want to do a nicer version of that.",
  "Any board game recommendations for two players? We mostly play cooperative games because we're both too competitive and it ends in sulking when we play against each other.",
  "He already has a lot of games though, like three full shelves of them, and I'm terrified of buying one he already owns or one he tried at a friend's place and didn't like.",
  "Thanks, I'll think about it. I'm leaning toward the board game café idea plus his favourite Thai place. Maybe I'll invite his brother too, since they don't see each other enough."],
 ["I took my bike in for a tune-up at the shop on 6th Avenue. They said the brake pads were pretty worn and the back wheel was slightly out of true, which explains a weird rubbing sound I kept hearing.",
  "They also said I should get wider tyres if I'm going to ride on the gravel trail along the water. Right now I mostly ride paved roads, but the gravel trail looks so nice on weekends.",
  "How often should I get it serviced? The shop was nice but not cheap, and I'd rather learn to do the basic stuff myself if it's not too hard and doesn't require a lot of special tools.",
  "I rode 20 miles last weekend! Out to Point Defiance and back, which is the farthest I've ridden in my adult life. My legs were jelly afterwards but I felt really proud of myself.",
  "I'm thinking about commuting by bike once a week. It's about six miles each way to the office with one nasty hill, and there's a shower at work, so it's actually pretty doable."],
 ["I signed up for a 10K in April, the one along Ruston Way. I've never run one before. The furthest I've ever run is maybe three miles, and that was years ago, so this is very much a stretch goal.",
  "How should I structure the weeks? I can realistically run three times a week, mornings before work, plus maybe a longer run on Saturdays if Theo walks Biscuit for me.",
  "My knees ache a bit after running, mostly the right one, on the outside. It's not sharp, more of a dull ache that goes away by the afternoon, but it worries me a little.",
  "What should I eat before a run? I usually run first thing in the morning on an empty stomach, and sometimes I feel a bit lightheaded halfway through, especially on the longer ones.",
  "Alright, three runs a week starting Monday. I'll put them in my calendar so I actually do them, and I'll check my shoes, which are probably older than my relationship with Theo."],
 ["My heating bill doubled this winter compared to last year. It's an older apartment with electric baseboard heaters, and I swear I can feel a breeze coming through the living room windows. Any ideas?",
  "We rent, so I can't change much, and the landlord is slow to fix anything. Last year it took him two months to replace a broken bathroom fan, so I'm not counting on new windows.",
  "Is a space heater cheaper? We mostly hang out in the living room in the evenings, and the bedroom only needs to be warm-ish at night, so heating the whole place seems wasteful.",
  "The windows are single pane, and the frames are old wood that doesn't close perfectly. In the morning there's condensation running down the inside of the glass.",
  "Okay, I'll try the window film this weekend. Theo is skeptical, but I'll show him the bill and I think he'll come around, especially if the living room actually feels warmer."],
 ["I got a used camera to take better photos on hikes, an older mirrorless one with a kit lens. My phone photos always look flat and the skies are white blobs, and I want to actually capture what it felt like being there.",
  "What settings should I use for waterfalls? I love the silky water look in other people's photos, but whenever I try, the whole picture comes out blurry or completely white.",
  "I don't have a tripod yet, and honestly I don't want to carry a big one on long hikes. My pack is already heavy enough with water, snacks and Biscuit's stuff.",
  "How do I avoid blown-out skies? It happens in almost every landscape shot I take, especially around midday when we usually hike, because that's when it's warmest.",
  "Thanks! We're going to Snoqualmie Falls next week, so I'll try everything there and see what comes out. I'll bring a cloth for the spray like you said."],
]
